<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> CaCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.147&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Sodium acetate                                          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.82&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>                                            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.142&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace element solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=243">243</a>)          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace vitamins (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197">197</a>)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Se/W solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=284">284</a>)                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;910.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v) gas mixture.  After cooling, add aseptically and anaerobically the following solutions (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized) to the medium:  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution*            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;30.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 1.0 M Sodium fumarate solution  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Iron(III) citrate solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1014">1014</a>)  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml   </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Adjust pH to 7.0-7.2, if necessary.  <br>
Comment: Iron(III) citrate solution can be replaced by Fe NTA solution (filter-sterilized, see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1355">1355</a>).       <br>
